2. **Leverage Information Asymmetry**: Gather intel on management’s priorities (e.g., cost-cutting, efficiency drives) and subtly leak partial truths. If they’re pushing for layoffs, hint that "some departments are underperforming" to shift blame away from their own missteps. 

